course: dictionary
lesson: 14708
title: Proceeding: going on and moving forward
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «proceeding» comes from the verb proceed, which means to go on or to move forward. When something is proceeding, it is not stopping. «The work is proceeding well» means the work is going on and getting done.
explain: You often meet this word in instructions and announcements. «Passengers are proceeding to gate 4» means the passengers should walk calmly on towards that gate. Proceed usually points to a place you are heading for.
explain: Grown-ups also use proceedings in a special way. «Legal proceedings» are the actions taken in a court, and proceedings can also mean the written record of a meeting. In everyday speech people say «going on» or «carrying on», so try those words in the sentence first.
fact: Proceed is the verb, and proceeding is the form that shows something is happening now.
fact: «Proceeding» means going on or continuing, as in «The work is proceeding well».
fact: «Proceeding» can also mean moving forward in a certain direction, as in «Passengers are proceeding to gate 4».
fact: «Proceedings» means the events of a meeting or ceremony, or legal action taken in a court.
fact: In everyday speech, say «going on» or «carrying on» instead of proceeding.
exercise: «The work is proceeding well.» What does proceeding mean here? | Breaking into pieces | Going backwards | Stopping for a long rest | *Going on, carrying on
exercise: «Passengers are proceeding to gate 4.» What does proceeding suggest? | Sitting down and waiting | Painting the gate | Running away from gate 4 | *Moving calmly forward towards gate 4
exercise: The news says «legal proceedings» have begun against the company. What are the proceedings? | A picnic in the park | A type of bread | *Legal action taken in a court | A kind of cloud
test: «The machine is proceeding slowly but safely.» Which word means the same as proceeding here? | Breaking | Sleeping | Hiding | *Continuing
test: «Please proceed to the exit.» What should you do? | Dance on the spot | Shout for help | *Walk calmly towards the exit | Stay in your seat
exam: «The secretary wrote down the proceedings of the meeting.» What are the proceedings? | *A written record of what happened at the meeting | A cold drink | Food served at the meeting | The chairs in the room
